          "review": "Take the open preconnected interval (-a,a), use the qualified order-(j+1) majorant with H=U=T>0, and set u(n)=4*spatialPrefactor(j+1,a,T)*gaussianMajorant(a,T,n). Gaussian summability and Summable.mul_left supply Summable u. The complete block derivative theorem supplies all n and every interior w, and the closed spatial strip includes (w,T). Summability of the order-j blocks at y supplies the required convergence witness, also at y. Thus every hypothesis of the pinned local hasDerivAt_tsum_of_isPreconnected is met and the result concerns the actual unconditional tsum, rather than a supplied abstract smooth function.",
