          "review": "Natural induction generalizes the evaluation point. The base is order zero. On the open interval neighborhood of y, the entire induction hypothesis gives equality of functions at every w, producing EventuallyEq at nhds y. iteratedDeriv_succ, the pinned EventuallyEq.deriv_eq, and the actual HasDerivAt.deriv identity then yield order j+1. No differentiation of a single-point equality occurs.",
