          "review": "The complete qualified order-j formula is promoted from pointwise identities to function equality by funext. Differentiating exp(-(c*w+k)/T) times the constant (-c/T)^j gives the order-(j+1) coefficient. The final proof normalizes pointwise negation, identity and c*1 before ring. All real c,k,T,y are valid; at T=0 real totalized division makes the exponential constant, so no missing nonzero-time hypothesis is needed for this finite-term statement.",
